            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF142 adds support for the dictionary property <code class=\"notranslate\">RTCRtpEncodingParameters.codec</code> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1894137\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1894137</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is used when setting encodings in <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCRtpSender/setParameters#encodings\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">RTCRtpSender.setParameters(parameter.encodings)</code></a> and <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCPeerConnection/addTransceiver#sendencodings\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">RTCPeerConnection.addTransceiver(sendencodings)</code></a>, and returned in <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCRtpSender/getParameters#encodings\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">RTCRtpSender/getParameters()</code></a> (<code class=\"notranslate\">encodings.codec</code>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release note.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3249074650\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40477\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40477/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40477\">#40477</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40631",
            "title": "FF142Relnote: RTCRtpSender.get/setParameters - encodings.codec property",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-05T02:46:27.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-05T02:44:22.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF142 adds support for the dictionary property <code class=\"notranslate\">RTCRtpEncodingParameters.codec</code> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1894137\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1894137</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is used when setting encodings in <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCRtpSender/setParameters#encodings\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">RTCRtpSender.setParameters(parameter.encodings)</code></a> and <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCPeerConnection/addTransceiver#sendencodings\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">RTCPeerConnection.addTransceiver(sendencodings)</code></a>, and returned in <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCRtpSender/getParameters#encodings\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">RTCRtpSender/getParameters()</code></a> (<code class=\"notranslate\">encodings.codec</code>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This updates the set/getParameters on the sender. The transceiver just references the sender, so doesn't need an update.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3249074650\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40477\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40477/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40477\">#40477</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40629",
            "title": "RTCRtpSender.get/setParameters - encodings.codec property",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-05T01:27:54.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-05T01:26:00.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112591951?u=83251e0d8e8f801faef99cc68533e148a728784b&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Clarify that <code class=\"notranslate\">backdrop-filter</code> only affects the backdrop image up to its nearest ancestor Backdrop Root as stated in the issue, and add a concise note listing what triggers a Backdrop Root which was obtained from the source listed in this PR.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">The existing text (“area behind an element”) implied that backdrop-filter applies to all pixels behind an element, which contradicts real-world behavior and the Filter Effects Level 2 specification. Developers encountered “missing” blur outside the nearest Backdrop Root (for example, a semi-transparent ancestor), leading to confusion. This update aligns MDN’s description with the spec and addresses user reports in the GitHub issue.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Filter Effects Level 2 (Backdrop Root definition)</strong><br>\n<a href=\"https://drafts.fxtf.org/filter-effects-2/#BackdropRoot\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://drafts.fxtf.org/filter-effects-2/#BackdropRoot</a></li>\n<li><strong>Live demo showing blur limited to the nearest Backdrop Root</strong><br>\n<a href=\"https://jsfiddle.net/xer31ywj/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://jsfiddle.net/xer31ywj/</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #40602.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3286769417\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40602\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40602/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40602\">#40602</a></p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40627",
            "title": "fix issue: Backdrop Root concept undocumented",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-04T20:38:52.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-04T20:36:33.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "kb42",
                "url": "https://github.com/kb42"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">After <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3207883044\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40228\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/40228/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40228\">#40228</a>, we are a lot more explicit on some CSS stylistic decisions. In particular, we now have systematic rules surrounding the preferred color notations. As a starter, I'm porting all colors that have named equivalents to named colors, per our recommendation of using \"common named colors\". Afterwards, I'm going to convert the remaining colors to the preferred notation, such as preferring <code class=\"notranslate\">rgb()</code> and preferring number parameters.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40624",
            "title": "Lint: use named color if possible (6)",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-05T13:54:10.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-04T16:40:48.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Josh-Cena",
                "url": "https://github.com/Josh-Cena"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">After <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3207883044\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40228\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/40228/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40228\">#40228</a>, we are a lot more explicit on some CSS stylistic decisions. In particular, we now have systematic rules surrounding the preferred color notations. As a starter, I'm porting all colors that have named equivalents to named colors, per our recommendation of using \"common named colors\". Afterwards, I'm going to convert the remaining colors to the preferred notation, such as preferring <code class=\"notranslate\">rgb()</code> and preferring number parameters.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40623",
            "title": "Lint: use named color if possible (5)",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-05T13:51:51.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-04T16:40:36.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Josh-Cena",
                "url": "https://github.com/Josh-Cena"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">After <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3207883044\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40228\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/40228/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40228\">#40228</a>, we are a lot more explicit on some CSS stylistic decisions. In particular, we now have systematic rules surrounding the preferred color notations. As a starter, I'm porting all colors that have named equivalents to named colors, per our recommendation of using \"common named colors\". Afterwards, I'm going to convert the remaining colors to the preferred notation, such as preferring <code class=\"notranslate\">rgb()</code> and preferring number parameters.</p>",
